VG.registerBibleChapters("genesis", [
{n:16, name:"The God Who Sees Me", seal:{ref:"Genesis 16:13",verse:"And she called the name of the LORD that spake unto her, Thou God seest me: for she said, Have I also here looked after him that seeth me?"}, facts:["Did you know Hagar is the only person in the Bible who gives God a name? After He found her in the wilderness, she called Him El roi, \"Thou God seest me\" (Genesis 16:13).","Did you know the name Ishmael means \"God hears\"? The angel chose it because the LORD had heard Hagar's affliction (Genesis 16:11).","Did you know the well where the angel met Hagar was named Beerlahairoi, \"the well of Him that liveth and seeth me,\" and it sat between Kadesh and Bered (Genesis 16:14)?"], questions:[
{q:"Why did Sarai give her handmaid Hagar to Abram as a wife?",options:["Because Sarai was barren and hoped to have children through Hagar","Because Abram had asked for another wife","Because Hagar had asked to marry Abram","Because Sarai wanted Hagar to leave the household"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:2",verse:"And Sarai said unto Abram, Behold now, the LORD hath restrained me from bearing: I pray thee, go in unto my maid; it may be that I may obtain children by her. And Abram hearkened to the voice of Sarai.",insight:"Sarai's plan came from her own barrenness, not from God's promise. When we try to hurry God's timing, we often create the very trouble we hoped to avoid."},
{q:"Who was Hagar?",options:["An Egyptian handmaid belonging to Sarai","A Canaanite princess visiting the camp","Abram's niece from Haran","A servant of Pharaoh's household"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:1",verse:"Now Sarai Abram’s wife bare him no children: and she had an handmaid, an Egyptian, whose name was Hagar.",insight:"Hagar was a foreign servant with no standing, yet God saw her. No one is too low or too far for the LORD to notice."},
{q:"How long had Abram lived in Canaan when Sarai gave him Hagar?",options:["Ten years","Seven years","Twelve years","Twenty years"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:3",verse:"And Sarai Abram’s wife took Hagar her maid the Egyptian, after Abram had dwelt ten years in the land of Canaan, and gave her to her husband Abram to be his wife.",insight:"Ten years of waiting wore Sarai down. Long delays test faith, and this chapter shows what happens when waiting turns into scheming."},
{q:"What changed between Sarai and Hagar after Hagar conceived?",options:["Hagar despised her mistress in her eyes","Hagar asked to be set free from service","Sarai raised Hagar to a place of honor","Hagar refused to serve Sarai any longer"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:4",verse:"And he went in unto Hagar, and she conceived: and when she saw that she had conceived, her mistress was despised in her eyes.",insight:"Blessing twisted into pride. The child Hagar carried was meant to help Sarai, but contempt poisoned the household instead."},
{q:"What did Sarai say to Abram about the wrong done to her?",options:["\"My wrong be upon thee\"","\"Send Hagar away at once\"","\"The LORD judge between me and thee\"","\"I will bear this wrong in silence\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:5",verse:"And Sarai said unto Abram, My wrong be upon thee: I have given my maid into thy bosom; and when she saw that she had conceived, I was despised in her eyes: the LORD judge between me and thee.",insight:"Sarai blamed Abram for the plan she herself proposed. It is easy to hand someone the scheme and then hand them the fault."},
{q:"How did Sarai treat Hagar after she conceived?",options:["She dealt hardly with her","She forgave her freely","She sold her to traders","She sent her back to Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:6",verse:"But Abram said unto Sarai, Behold, thy maid is in thy hand; do to her as it pleaseth thee. And when Sarai dealt hardly with her, she fled from her face.",insight:"Harshness answered contempt, and the home filled with strife. Hard dealings never heal a household; they scatter it."},
{q:"What did Hagar do under Sarai's harsh dealing?",options:["She fled from Sarai's face","She appealed to Abram for justice","She hid inside Abram's tent","She set out for Egypt on foot"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:6",verse:"But Abram said unto Sarai, Behold, thy maid is in thy hand; do to her as it pleaseth thee. And when Sarai dealt hardly with her, she fled from her face.",insight:"Hagar ran toward the wilderness with nowhere to go. God often meets us on the road we take when we feel we cannot stay."},
{q:"Where did the angel of the LORD find Hagar?",options:["By a fountain of water in the wilderness, on the way to Shur","At the gate of Abram's camp","In the city of Beersheba","By the river of Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:7",verse:"And the angel of the LORD found her by a fountain of water in the wilderness, by the fountain in the way to Shur.",insight:"The angel found her; she did not find Him. Grace seeks the runaway before the runaway seeks grace."},
{q:"What was the angel's first question to Hagar?",options:["\"Whence camest thou? and whither wilt thou go?\"","\"Why hast thou left thy mistress?\"","\"Dost thou know the way to Egypt?\"","\"Wilt thou return to Abram's house?\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:8",verse:"And he said, Hagar, Sarai’s maid, whence camest thou? and whither wilt thou go? And she said, I flee from the face of my mistress Sarai.",insight:"God asked where she came from and where she was going. Honest questions from God help us face where we truly are."},
{q:"How did Hagar answer the angel?",options:["\"I flee from the face of my mistress Sarai\"","\"I go to find my own people\"","\"I seek a new master in Egypt\"","\"I do not know where I am going\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:8",verse:"And he said, Hagar, Sarai’s maid, whence camest thou? and whither wilt thou go? And she said, I flee from the face of my mistress Sarai.",insight:"Hagar told the plain truth about her running. God can work with honesty, even when the story is messy."},
{q:"What did the angel command Hagar to do?",options:["Return to her mistress and submit herself under her hands","Continue to Egypt and live as a free woman","Wait at the well until Abram came for her","Go and live apart in the wilderness"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:9",verse:"And the angel of the LORD said unto her, Return to thy mistress, and submit thyself under her hands.",insight:"The command was not escape but return and submit. Sometimes obedience leads back into the hard place, with God's promise going with us."},
{q:"What did the angel promise about Hagar's descendants?",options:["They would be multiplied exceedingly, too many to be numbered","They would inherit the land of Canaan","They would serve in Abram's house forever","They would return to rule in Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:10",verse:"And the angel of the LORD said unto her, I will multiply thy seed exceedingly, that it shall not be numbered for multitude.",insight:"To a runaway servant God gave the same kind of promise He gave Abram: countless descendants. God's generosity is not reserved for the prominent."},
{q:"What name was Hagar told to give her son?",options:["Ishmael","Isaac","Midian","Jokshan"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:11",verse:"And the angel of the LORD said unto her, Behold, thou art with child, and shalt bear a son, and shalt call his name Ishmael; because the LORD hath heard thy affliction.",insight:"Ishmael means \"God hears.\" Before the child was even born, his name preached that God had heard his mother's affliction."},
{q:"Why was the child to be named Ishmael?",options:["Because the LORD had heard Hagar's affliction","Because he would be Abram's firstborn son","Because the name would honor Sarai","Because it was the custom of Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:11",verse:"And the angel of the LORD said unto her, Behold, thou art with child, and shalt bear a son, and shalt call his name Ishmael; because the LORD hath heard thy affliction.",insight:"God named the boy after what He had done: heard. When God hears affliction, He answers with a name and a future."},
{q:"How did the angel describe Ishmael's future?",options:["A wild man; his hand against every man, and every man's hand against him","A quiet child who would love peace","A shepherd who would dwell in tents","A prince who would rule many cities"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:12",verse:"And he will be a wild man; his hand will be against every man, and every man’s hand against him; and he shall dwell in the presence of all his brethren.",insight:"The prophecy was frank about the strife ahead. God tells the truth about the future, even the hard parts, so we can trust Him in it."},
{q:"What name did Hagar give to the LORD who spoke to her?",options:["\"Thou God seest me,\" El roi","\"The God of Abram\"","\"The LORD my shepherd\"","\"The God of the wilderness\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:13",verse:"And she called the name of the LORD that spake unto her, Thou God seest me: for she said, Have I also here looked after him that seeth me?",insight:"A servant girl named God \"the One who sees me.\" To be seen by God in our lowest place is the beginning of hope."},
{q:"What was the well called where the angel met Hagar?",options:["Beerlahairoi","Beersheba","Rehoboth","Sitnah"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:14",verse:"Wherefore the well was called Beer-lahai-roi; behold, it is between Kadesh and Bered.",insight:"Beerlahairoi means \"the well of Him that liveth and seeth me.\" Hagar left a marker so others would know that God sees the afflicted."},
{q:"Where was the well Beerlahairoi located?",options:["Between Kadesh and Bered","Between Bethel and Ai","Beside the oaks of Mamre","At the border of Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:14",verse:"Wherefore the well was called Beer-lahai-roi; behold, it is between Kadesh and Bered.",insight:"The place got a name because God met someone there. Ordinary ground becomes holy when God shows up."},
{q:"Who gave Abram's son the name Ishmael at his birth?",options:["Abram called his son's name Ishmael","Sarai chose the name alone","The angel named him at the birth","Hagar named him without Abram"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:15",verse:"And Hagar bare Abram a son: and Abram called his son’s name, which Hagar bare, Ishmael.",insight:"Abram kept the name the angel had given. Obedience sometimes means keeping God's word even when the circumstances are complicated."},
{q:"How old was Abram when Hagar bore him Ishmael?",options:["Eighty-six years old","Seventy-five years old","Ninety-nine years old","One hundred years old"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 16:16",verse:"And Abram was fourscore and six years old, when Hagar bare Ishmael to Abram.",insight:"At eighty-six Abram held his first son, yet Isaac was still thirteen years away. God's promise was not finished; it was only unfolding."}
]},
{n:17, name:"The Covenant Sealed", seal:{ref:"Genesis 17:19",verse:"And God said, Sarah thy wife shall bear thee a son indeed; and thou shalt call his name Isaac: and I will establish my covenant with him for an everlasting covenant, and with his seed after him."}, facts:["Did you know God commanded circumcision on the eighth day, long before anyone understood why? The sign of the covenant was given when a man child was eight days old (Genesis 17:12).","Did you know Abraham was ninety-nine and Ishmael thirteen when they were circumcised? The whole household obeyed on the very same day (Genesis 17:24-26).","Did you know the name Abraham means \"father of a multitude of nations\"? God renamed Abram before the promised son was even conceived (Genesis 17:5)."], questions:[
{q:"How old was Abram when the LORD appeared to him in this chapter?",options:["Ninety-nine years old","Eighty-six years old","One hundred years old","Seventy-five years old"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:1",verse:"And when Abram was ninety years old and nine, the LORD appeared to Abram, and said unto him, I am the Almighty God; walk before me, and be thou perfect.",insight:"Thirteen years after Ishmael's birth, God came again. God's silence is not God's absence; He returns right on time."},
{q:"What did God say He would do for Abram?",options:["Make His covenant with him and multiply him exceedingly","Give him a new land beyond the river","Make him a priest to the nations","Give him rest from all his enemies"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:2",verse:"And I will make my covenant between me and thee, and will multiply thee exceedingly.",insight:"Covenant and multiplication: God commits Himself before asking anything. His promises rest on His character, not our performance."},
{q:"By what name did God reveal Himself to Abram here?",options:["God Almighty","The LORD of hosts","The Most High God","The Everlasting God"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:1",verse:"And when Abram was ninety years old and nine, the LORD appeared to Abram, and said unto him, I am the Almighty God; walk before me, and be thou perfect.",insight:"El Shaddai, God Almighty. The name fit the promise: only an Almighty God could give a child to the childless."},
{q:"What new name did God give Abram?",options:["Abraham","Israel","Judah","Emmanuel"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:5",verse:"Neither shall thy name any more be called Abram, but thy name shall be Abraham; for a father of many nations have I made thee.",insight:"Abram became Abraham while still childless by Sarah. God names us for the future He is making, not the past we have lived."},
{q:"Why did God change his name to Abraham?",options:["Because He had made him a father of many nations","Because he had left his father's house","Because he had believed God's word","Because he was now a great prince"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:5",verse:"Neither shall thy name any more be called Abram, but thy name shall be Abraham; for a father of many nations have I made thee.",insight:"The new name was a promise spoken as a fact. Faith learns to live inside God's \"already\" before we see it."},
{q:"What did God promise to make of Abraham?",options:["Exceeding fruitful; nations and kings would come from him","A mighty warrior among men","A wealthy trader of the east","A ruler over all his servants"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:6",verse:"And I will make thee exceeding fruitful, and I will make nations of thee, and kings shall come out of thee.",insight:"Fruitfulness, nations, kings: the promise kept widening. God's plans for us are always larger than our asking."},
{q:"What did God promise to give Abraham and his seed?",options:["All the land of Canaan, for an everlasting possession","The city of Haran and its fields","The treasures of Egypt","The hills of Seir"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:8",verse:"And I will give unto thee, and to thy seed after thee, the land wherein thou art a stranger, all the land of Canaan, for an everlasting possession; and I will be their God.",insight:"The land was a gift tied to the covenant, not a wage for good behavior. Inheritance in God's family is received, not earned."},
{q:"What was the token of the covenant?",options:["Circumcision","A burnt offering","A stone pillar","A rainbow in the cloud"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:11",verse:"And ye shall circumcise the flesh of your foreskin; and it shall be a token of the covenant betwixt me and you.",insight:"The covenant was cut into the flesh as a permanent reminder. God marks His people so they never forget whose they are."},
{q:"At what age was every man child to be circumcised?",options:["When he was eight days old","On the day he was born","When he was thirteen years old","When he became a man"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:12",verse:"And he that is eight days old shall be circumcised among you, every man child in your generations, he that is born in the house, or bought with money of any stranger, which is not of thy seed.",insight:"Eight days old: the sign came before understanding. God's covenant reaches us before we can reach for it."},
{q:"Besides sons born in the house, who else had to be circumcised?",options:["Every servant bought with money, even a foreigner","Only the firstborn sons","Only those who chose it freely","Only the sons of Sarah"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:13",verse:"He that is born in thy house, and he that is bought with thy money, must needs be circumcised: and my covenant shall be in your flesh for an everlasting covenant.",insight:"The covenant swept in the whole household, bought or born. No one under Abraham's roof was left outside God's sign."},
{q:"What would happen to the uncircumcised man child?",options:["He would be cut off from his people, having broken the covenant","He would be sold as a servant","He would be sent out of the camp","He would lose his inheritance"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:14",verse:"And the uncircumcised man child whose flesh of his foreskin is not circumcised, that soul shall be cut off from his people; he hath broken my covenant.",insight:"Refusing the sign meant refusing the covenant. God is gracious, but His covenant still asks for our yes."},
{q:"What new name did God give Sarai?",options:["Sarah","Rebekah","Rachel","Milcah"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:15",verse:"And God said unto Abraham, As for Sarai thy wife, thou shalt not call her name Sarai, but Sarah shall her name be.",insight:"Sarai became Sarah, from \"my princess\" to \"princess\" of nations. God enlarged her name as He enlarged her future."},
{q:"What did God say Sarah would become?",options:["A mother of nations; kings of people would come from her","A queen ruling in Egypt","A prophetess to the nations","The mother of twelve princes"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:16",verse:"And I will bless her, and give thee a son also of her: yea, I will bless her, and she shall be a mother of nations; kings of people shall be of her.",insight:"A barren old woman was named mother of nations. God's promises delight in doing the impossible through the unlikely."},
{q:"How did Abraham respond when God said Sarah would bear a son?",options:["He fell on his face and laughed","He wept for joy","He argued with God","He ran to tell Sarah"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:17",verse:"Then Abraham fell upon his face, and laughed, and said in his heart, Shall a child be born unto him that is an hundred years old? and shall Sarah, that is ninety years old, bear?",insight:"Laughter of disbelief, face down in worship at once. God can handle our amazed laughter while we are still bowing."},
{q:"What did Abraham say in his heart?",options:["\"Shall a child be born unto him that is an hundred years old? and shall Sarah, that is ninety years old, bear?\"","\"How shall this be, seeing I know not the time?\"","\"Wilt thou indeed give me a son in my old age?\"","\"Is Sarah not too old for thy promise?\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:17",verse:"Then Abraham fell upon his face, and laughed, and said in his heart, Shall a child be born unto him that is an hundred years old? and shall Sarah, that is ninety years old, bear?",insight:"Abraham did the math and it failed. Faith begins where our calculations end."},
{q:"What name was the promised son to be given?",options:["Isaac","Ishmael","Jacob","Joseph"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:19",verse:"And God said, Sarah thy wife shall bear thee a son indeed; and thou shalt call his name Isaac: and I will establish my covenant with him for an everlasting covenant, and with his seed after him.",insight:"Isaac means \"laughter.\" God named the promised child after Abraham's laugh, turning disbelief into joy."},
{q:"When would Sarah bear Isaac?",options:["At the set time in the next year","Before the winter rains","When Abraham was one hundred","After Ishmael left home"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:21",verse:"But my covenant will I establish with Isaac, which Sarah shall bear unto thee at this set time in the next year.",insight:"God set the time: next year. Promises with deadlines teach us that God is never vague about His faithfulness."},
{q:"What did God promise concerning Ishmael?",options:["He would bless him, make him fruitful, and make him a great nation with twelve princes","He would inherit the covenant with Isaac","He would be sent away empty","He would become a servant to Isaac"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:20",verse:"And as for Ishmael, I have heard thee: Behold, I have blessed him, and will make him fruitful, and will multiply him exceedingly; twelve princes shall he beget, and I will make him a great nation.",insight:"Ishmael was not the child of promise, but he was still blessed. God's \"no\" to one role is never His \"nothing\" to the person."},
{q:"On what day were Abraham and his household circumcised?",options:["The very same day God commanded it","A week later","At the next new moon","After Isaac was born"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:23",verse:"And Abraham took Ishmael his son, and all that were born in his house, and all that were bought with his money, every male among the men of Abraham’s house; and circumcised the flesh of their foreskin in the selfsame day, as God had said unto him.",insight:"Abraham did not delay. The selfsame day: prompt obedience is the truest answer to God's voice."},
{q:"How old was Ishmael when he was circumcised?",options:["Thirteen years old","Eight days old","Nineteen years old","Thirty years old"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 17:25",verse:"And Ishmael his son was thirteen years old, when he was circumcised in the flesh of his foreskin.",insight:"Ishmael bore the sign too. God's covenant kindness reached beyond the child of promise to the whole household."}
]},
{n:18, name:"Visitors at Mamre", seal:{ref:"Genesis 18:14",verse:"Is any thing too hard for the LORD? At the time appointed I will return unto thee, according to the time of life, and Sarah shall have a son."}, facts:["Did you know the question \"Is any thing too hard for the LORD?\" is first asked in this chapter, when Sarah laughed at the promise of a son in her old age (Genesis 18:14)?","Did you know Abraham bargained with God from fifty righteous down to ten, and God agreed every single time (Genesis 18:26-32)?","Did you know Abraham served his visitors bread, butter, milk, and a tender calf, and stood by them under the tree while they ate (Genesis 18:7-8)?"], questions:[
{q:"Where did the LORD appear to Abraham?",options:["In the plains of Mamre","At the oaks of Moreh","On the hill of Bethel","In the valley of Gerar"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:1",verse:"And the LORD appeared unto him in the plains of Mamre: and he sat in the tent door in the heat of the day;",insight:"God came to Abraham's tent, not a temple. The LORD still visits ordinary places where His people dwell."},
{q:"What was Abraham doing when the visitors came?",options:["Sitting in the tent door in the heat of the day","Tending his flocks in the field","Praying at his altar","Sleeping inside his tent"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:1",verse:"And the LORD appeared unto him in the plains of Mamre: and he sat in the tent door in the heat of the day;",insight:"In the heat of the day, at rest, Abraham was ready. Readiness for God is a posture we keep even in quiet hours."},
{q:"How many men did Abraham see standing by him?",options:["Three","Two","Seven","Twelve"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:2",verse:"And he lift up his eyes and looked, and, lo, three men stood by him: and when he saw them, he ran to meet them from the tent door, and bowed himself toward the ground,",insight:"Three visitors, one of them the LORD. God often comes to us in ways we only understand afterward."},
{q:"What did Abraham do when he saw them?",options:["He ran to meet them and bowed himself toward the ground","He sent his servant to greet them","He called Sarah to come quickly","He offered them gifts of silver"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:2",verse:"And he lift up his eyes and looked, and, lo, three men stood by him: and when he saw them, he ran to meet them from the tent door, and bowed himself toward the ground,",insight:"Abraham ran. Reverence that hurries is love in motion; he treated strangers like honored guests."},
{q:"What did Abraham ask them to allow?",options:["That a little water be fetched to wash their feet","That they stay with him seven days","That they bless his household","That they share news from afar"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:4",verse:"Let a little water, I pray you, be fetched, and wash your feet, and rest yourselves under the tree:",insight:"Hospitality began with water for dusty feet. Small kindnesses open the door to great encounters."},
{q:"What did Abraham ask Sarah to prepare?",options:["Cakes from three measures of fine meal","A stew of lentils","Unleavened bread only","A basket of figs"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:6",verse:"And Abraham hastened into the tent unto Sarah, and said, Make ready quickly three measures of fine meal, knead it, and make cakes upon the hearth.",insight:"Three measures of fine meal, the best flour, quickly made. When God visits, we bring our finest without delay."},
{q:"What meat did Abraham fetch for the meal?",options:["A calf tender and good","A lamb from the flock","A young goat","Two turtledoves"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:7",verse:"And Abraham ran unto the herd, and fetcht a calf tender and good, and gave it unto a young man; and he hasted to dress it.",insight:"Not the leftover, the tender calf. Worship gives God the choice portion, not the convenient one."},
{q:"Besides the calf, what did Abraham set before them?",options:["Butter and milk","Wine and honey","Bread and oil","Cheese and fruit"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:8",verse:"And he took butter, and milk, and the calf which he had dressed, and set it before them; and he stood by them under the tree, and they did eat.",insight:"Butter, milk, and the calf: a full table. Abraham's generosity pictures how God spreads His own table for us."},
{q:"What did the visitors ask Abraham?",options:["\"Where is Sarah thy wife?\"","\"Where are thy servants?\"","\"How many sons hast thou?\"","\"Where is thy nephew Lot?\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:9",verse:"And they said unto him, Where is Sarah thy wife? And he said, Behold, in the tent.",insight:"The question drew Sarah into the promise. God makes His promises personal, naming names."},
{q:"What did the visitor promise Abraham?",options:["He would return at the time of life, and Sarah would have a son","Abraham's wealth would be doubled","Lot would be delivered from Sodom","Ishmael would be greatly blessed"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:10",verse:"And he said, I will certainly return unto thee according to the time of life; and, lo, Sarah thy wife shall have a son. And Sarah heard it in the tent door, which was behind him.",insight:"A date was set: the time of life. God's promises are not wishes; they come with His appointed time."},
{q:"How did Sarah react to the promise?",options:["She laughed within herself","She wept with joy","She ran to embrace Abraham","She doubted aloud before them"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:12",verse:"Therefore Sarah laughed within herself, saying, After I am waxed old shall I have pleasure, my lord being old also?",insight:"Sarah laughed inside, thinking no one heard. God hears even our silent laughter and answers it with grace."},
{q:"Why did Sarah think the promise impossible?",options:["She was past the age of childbearing, and her lord was old also","She had been barren only a short time","She feared the journey ahead","She believed the visitor was joking"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:12",verse:"Therefore Sarah laughed within herself, saying, After I am waxed old shall I have pleasure, my lord being old also?",insight:"Sarah measured God's promise by her body's calendar. Faith must learn a new arithmetic, where God's power is the only number that matters."},
{q:"What did the LORD ask Abraham?",options:["\"Wherefore did Sarah laugh?\"","\"Why dost thou doubt my word?\"","\"Wherefore is Sarah afraid?\"","\"Doth Sarah believe my promise?\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:13",verse:"And the LORD said unto Abraham, Wherefore did Sarah laugh, saying, Shall I of a surety bear a child, which am old?",insight:"God named the laugh. He confronts our unbelief gently but directly, because hidden doubt cannot be healed."},
{q:"What great question did the LORD then ask?",options:["\"Is any thing too hard for the LORD?\"","\"Is my arm shortened that it cannot save?\"","\"Who hath believed our report?\"","\"Shall I hide my counsel from thee?\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:14",verse:"Is any thing too hard for the LORD? At the time appointed I will return unto thee, according to the time of life, and Sarah shall have a son.",insight:"This question still echoes over every impossible situation. Nothing is too hard for the LORD, then or now."},
{q:"What did Sarah do when confronted about laughing?",options:["She denied it, saying \"I laughed not,\" because she was afraid","She confessed and wept","She laughed openly","She left the tent"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:15",verse:"Then Sarah denied, saying, I laughed not; for she was afraid. And he said, Nay; but thou didst laugh.",insight:"Fear made Sarah deny. God did not crush her for it; He simply told the truth and kept His promise."},
{q:"How did the LORD answer her denial?",options:["\"Nay; but thou didst laugh\"","\"Peace, daughter, thy faith is enough\"","\"Go and doubt no more\"","\"Thy fear is forgiven thee\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:15",verse:"Then Sarah denied, saying, I laughed not; for she was afraid. And he said, Nay; but thou didst laugh.",insight:"Four words, firm and kind. God corrects without condemning, and His correction carries us toward faith."},
{q:"When the men rose to go, toward what city did they look?",options:["Sodom","Gomorrah","Zoar","Salem"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:16",verse:"And the men rose up from thence, and looked toward Sodom: and Abraham went with them to bring them on the way.",insight:"Their faces turned toward judgment while Abraham stood with mercy. Intercession begins when we see where the world is heading."},
{q:"What did the LORD say He had heard from Sodom and Gomorrah?",options:["Their cry is great, and their sin very grievous","Lot had prayed for the city","The angels would test the city","Abraham should warn the city"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:20",verse:"And the LORD said, Because the cry of Sodom and Gomorrah is great, and because their sin is very grievous;",insight:"The cry of the oppressed reached heaven. God hears the suffering that sin causes, and He acts."},
{q:"What did Abraham declare about God as Judge?",options:["\"Shall not the Judge of all the earth do right?\"","\"Wilt thou destroy the righteous with the wicked?\"","\"Shall thy mercy endure forever?\"","\"Wilt thou not spare thy servant Lot?\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:25",verse:"That be far from thee to do after this manner, to slay the righteous with the wicked: and that the righteous should be as the wicked, that be far from thee: Shall not the Judge of all the earth do right?",insight:"Abraham appealed to God's own character. The Judge of all the earth cannot do wrong, and prayer may boldly say so."},
{q:"To what number did Abraham finally bring his plea for Sodom?",options:["Ten righteous","Five righteous","Twenty righteous","Fifty righteous"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 18:32",verse:"And he said, Oh let not the Lord be angry, and I will speak yet but this once: Peradventure ten shall be found there. And he said, I will not destroy it for ten’s sake.",insight:"From fifty to ten, God said yes every time. Bold, humble prayer moves the heart of God, and He welcomes it."}
]},
{n:19, name:"Sodom and Gomorrah", seal:{ref:"Genesis 19:24",verse:"Then the LORD rained upon Sodom and upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire from the LORD out of heaven;"}, facts:["Did you know Lot's wife became a pillar of salt for one backward glance, after being clearly told not to look back (Genesis 19:26)?","Did you know Zoar was spared only because Lot begged to flee there? He called it \"a little one,\" and the angels granted his request (Genesis 19:20-22).","Did you know the Moabites and Ammonites, Israel's long-time neighbors, trace their beginning to Lot's daughters in this chapter (Genesis 19:37-38)?"], questions:[
{q:"How many angels came to Sodom at evening?",options:["Two","Three","One","Seven"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:1",verse:"And there came two angels to Sodom at even; and Lot sat in the gate of Sodom: and Lot seeing them rose up to meet them; and he bowed himself with his face toward the ground;",insight:"Two angels, no crowd. God does not need many to accomplish His purpose in a city."},
{q:"Where was Lot when the angels arrived?",options:["Sitting in the gate of Sodom","Tending sheep in the field","Praying at his tent door","Trading in the marketplace"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:1",verse:"And there came two angels to Sodom at even; and Lot sat in the gate of Sodom: and Lot seeing them rose up to meet them; and he bowed himself with his face toward the ground;",insight:"Lot sat in the gate, a place of influence, yet his influence could not save the city. Position without righteousness changes nothing."},
{q:"What did Lot urge the angels to do?",options:["Turn in, tarry all night, and lodge in his house","Flee the city before morning","Go and warn the men of Sodom","Rest at the city inn"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:2",verse:"And he said, Behold now, my lords, turn in, I pray you, into your servant’s house, and tarry all night, and wash your feet, and ye shall rise up early, and go on your ways. And they said, Nay; but we will abide in the street all night.",insight:"Lot pressed hospitality on strangers, like his uncle Abraham. Kindness to strangers is a family trait worth keeping."},
{q:"Who surrounded Lot's house that night?",options:["The men of Sodom, both old and young, from every quarter","The elders of the city only","A band of robbers","The servants of the king"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:4",verse:"But before they lay down, the men of the city, even the men of Sodom, compassed the house round, both old and young, all the people from every quarter:",insight:"Old and young, from every quarter: the corruption was total. When a whole culture turns, judgment is near."},
{q:"What did the mob demand?",options:["\"Bring them out unto us, that we may know them\"","\"Send these strangers away\"","\"Pay us tribute for lodging\"","\"Tell us whence they came\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:5",verse:"And they called unto Lot, and said unto him, Where are the men which came in to thee this night? bring them out unto us, that we may know them.",insight:"Their demand exposed the city's heart. Sin that is celebrated openly is sin ripe for judgment."},
{q:"What did Lot offer the mob instead?",options:["His two virgin daughters","His flocks and herds","All his silver and gold","Himself as their prisoner"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:8",verse:"Behold now, I have two daughters which have not known man; let me, I pray you, bring them out unto you, and do ye to them as is good in your eyes: only unto these men do nothing; for therefore came they under the shadow of my roof.",insight:"Lot's offer was terribly wrong, trading his daughters' safety for his guests'. Even righteous Lot shows how living in Sodom had warped his judgment."},
{q:"How did the mob answer Lot?",options:["\"Stand back\"","\"We accept thy offer\"","\"Bring them out quickly\"","\"Begone from our city\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:9",verse:"And they said, Stand back. And they said again, This one fellow came in to sojourn, and he will needs be a judge: now will we deal worse with thee, than with them. And they pressed sore upon the man, even Lot, and came near to break the door.",insight:"\"Stand back\": the wicked silencing the righteous. A society that shouts down conscience is far down the road."},
{q:"What did the angels do to the men at the door?",options:["They smote them with blindness, both small and great","They struck them with leprosy","They bound them with chains","They drove them with a great wind"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:11",verse:"And they smote the men that were at the door of the house with blindness, both small and great: so that they wearied themselves to find the door.",insight:"Blindness for those who would do evil. God still blinds the schemes of the wicked to protect His own."},
{q:"Whom did the angels tell Lot to gather out of the city?",options:["His sons-in-law, sons, daughters, and all he had in the city","His servants and cattle","The righteous men of Sodom","The elders of the gate"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:12",verse:"And the men said unto Lot, Hast thou here any besides? son in law, and thy sons, and thy daughters, and whatsoever thou hast in the city, bring them out of this place:",insight:"God's rescue reached for Lot's whole family. Mercy always wants to save more, not fewer."},
{q:"Why were the angels about to destroy the city?",options:["Because its cry had grown great before the LORD","Because Lot had prayed for judgment","Because Abraham had asked it","Because the king had rebelled"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:13",verse:"For we will destroy this place, because the cry of them is waxen great before the face of the LORD; and the LORD hath sent us to destroy it.",insight:"The cry of Sodom's victims reached heaven. God judges because He hears the cries that the powerful ignore."},
{q:"How did Lot's sons-in-law take his warning?",options:["He seemed to them as one that mocked","They believed and fled at once","They asked him for proof","They reported him to the elders"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:14",verse:"And Lot went out, and spake unto his sons in law, which married his daughters, and said, Up, get you out of this place; for the LORD will destroy this city. But he seemed as one that mocked unto his sons in law.",insight:"They thought he was joking. A righteous life lived too quietly in a wicked place loses its warning voice."},
{q:"What did the angels urge at daybreak?",options:["\"Arise, take thy wife and thy two daughters, lest thou be consumed\"","\"Hide in the mountains today\"","\"Gather thy goods and follow us\"","\"Warn the city once more\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:15",verse:"And when the morning arose, then the angels hastened Lot, saying, Arise, take thy wife, and thy two daughters, which are here; lest thou be consumed in the iniquity of the city.",insight:"Morning mercies: God hurried Lot out of danger. When God says arise, delay is disobedience."},
{q:"Why did the angels lay hold on Lot's hand?",options:["The LORD being merciful unto him","Because Lot was blind","Because he refused to walk","Because the way was steep"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:16",verse:"And while he lingered, the men laid hold upon his hand, and upon the hand of his wife, and upon the hand of his two daughters; the LORD being merciful unto him: and they brought him forth, and set him without the city.",insight:"Lot lingered, so mercy took his hand. When we are slow to obey, God in kindness sometimes drags us toward safety."},
{q:"What command came as they fled the city?",options:["\"Escape for thy life; look not behind thee\"","\"Run to the mountains quickly\"","\"Take nothing with thee\"","\"Weep not for the city\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:17",verse:"And it came to pass, when they had brought them forth abroad, that he said, Escape for thy life; look not behind thee, neither stay thou in all the plain; escape to the mountain, lest thou be consumed.",insight:"Do not look back. Rescue requires a forward heart; longing for what God is judging will destroy us."},
{q:"Where did Lot beg permission to flee?",options:["To Zoar, which he called \"a little one\"","To the mountains of Moab","To the city of Salem","To Abraham's camp"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:20",verse:"Behold now, this city is near to flee unto, and it is a little one: Oh, let me escape thither, (is it not a little one?) and my soul shall live.",insight:"Lot bargained for a small city instead of the mountains God named. God granted it, showing patience with our small faith."},
{q:"What did the LORD rain upon Sodom and Gomorrah?",options:["Brimstone and fire out of heaven","Hailstones and lightning","A great flood of waters","Burning coals of juniper"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:24",verse:"Then the LORD rained upon Sodom and upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire from the LORD out of heaven;",insight:"Fire from heaven: judgment was certain and total. God is patient, but His patience is not permission."},
{q:"What happened to Lot's wife?",options:["She looked back and became a pillar of salt","She was consumed by the fire","She was turned to stone","She was left behind weeping"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:26",verse:"But his wife looked back from behind him, and she became a pillar of salt.",insight:"One backward look cost her everything. Her heart was still in Sodom, and her eyes followed her heart."},
{q:"What did Abraham see when he looked toward Sodom in the morning?",options:["The smoke of the land going up like the smoke of a furnace","The cities standing unharmed","The angels returning to heaven","A great cloud of dust"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:28",verse:"And he looked toward Sodom and Gomorrah, and toward all the land of the plain, and beheld, and, lo, the smoke of the country went up as the smoke of a furnace.",insight:"Abraham saw the smoke of answered intercession's limit. He had prayed, God had heard, and justice still fell where no righteous were found."},
{q:"What did Lot's daughters plan in order to preserve their family?",options:["To make their father drink wine and lie with him, to preserve seed","To find husbands in Zoar","To return to Abraham's house","To build an altar and pray"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:32",verse:"Come, let us make our father drink wine, and we will lie with him, that we may preserve seed of our father.",insight:"Raised in Sodom, the daughters schemed with Sodom's morals. The company we keep shapes the choices we imagine."},
{q:"What were the names of the two sons born to Lot's daughters?",options:["Moab and Benammi","Esau and Jacob","Perez and Zerah","Moab and Ammon"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 19:37",verse:"And the firstborn bare a son, and called his name Moab: the same is the father of the Moabites unto this day.",insight:"Moab and Benammi: names born of a shameful night became nations in history. God writes straight with crooked lines, but the crookedness still costs."}
]},
{n:20, name:"Abraham and Abimelech", seal:{ref:"Genesis 20:7",verse:"Now therefore restore the man his wife; for he is a prophet, and he shall pray for thee, and thou shalt live: and if thou restore her not, know thou that thou shalt surely die, thou, and all that are thine."}, facts:["Did you know the word \"prophet\" appears here for the first time in the Bible? God called Abraham a prophet when warning Abimelech (Genesis 20:7).","Did you know Abimelech paid a thousand pieces of silver as \"a covering of the eyes,\" a public payment clearing Sarah's honor (Genesis 20:16)?","Did you know God had closed every womb in Abimelech's household because of Sarah, and opened them again when Abraham prayed (Genesis 20:17-18)?"], questions:[
{q:"In what city did Abraham sojourn?",options:["Gerar","Beersheba","Hebron","Salem"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:1",verse:"And Abraham journeyed from thence toward the south country, and dwelled between Kadesh and Shur, and sojourned in Gerar.",insight:"Abraham sojourned in Gerar, living as a stranger among strangers. God's people have always been travelers here."},
{q:"Between which two places had Abraham dwelt before Gerar?",options:["Kadesh and Shur","Bethel and Ai","Dan and Beersheba","Haran and Canaan"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:1",verse:"And Abraham journeyed from thence toward the south country, and dwelled between Kadesh and Shur, and sojourned in Gerar.",insight:"Between Kadesh and Shur: even the geography reminds us Abraham lived on the move, trusting God for the next step."},
{q:"Who was Abimelech?",options:["King of Gerar","Pharaoh of Egypt","King of Salem","Prince of the Philistines"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:2",verse:"And Abraham said of Sarah his wife, She is my sister: and Abimelech king of Gerar sent, and took Sarah.",insight:"A king with power over Abraham's household, yet under God's hand. No earthly power stands outside God's reach."},
{q:"What did Abraham say about Sarah in Gerar?",options:["\"She is my sister\"","\"She is my servant\"","\"She is a widow\"","\"She is my cousin\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:2",verse:"And Abraham said of Sarah his wife, She is my sister: and Abimelech king of Gerar sent, and took Sarah.",insight:"Fear made Abraham bend the truth again. Old failures revisit us until we face them with God."},
{q:"How did God come to Abimelech?",options:["In a dream by night","In a vision at noon","Through a prophet's message","In a whirlwind"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:3",verse:"But God came to Abimelech in a dream by night, and said to him, Behold, thou art but a dead man, for the woman which thou hast taken; for she is a man’s wife.",insight:"God spoke to a pagan king in a dream. The LORD can get anyone's attention, anywhere, to protect His own."},
{q:"What did God say to Abimelech in the dream?",options:["\"Behold, thou art but a dead man, for the woman thou hast taken; for she is a man's wife\"","\"Restore the woman sevenfold\"","\"Leave my servant's house\"","\"Pay a ransom for thy life\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:3",verse:"But God came to Abimelech in a dream by night, and said to him, Behold, thou art but a dead man, for the woman which thou hast taken; for she is a man’s wife.",insight:"Blunt and merciful at once: a death sentence with a way out. God's warnings are kindnesses dressed as thunder."},
{q:"What did Abimelech plead?",options:["\"Lord, wilt thou slay also a righteous nation?\"","\"Have mercy on thy servant\"","\"I knew not the law\"","\"Spare me for my people's sake\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:4",verse:"But Abimelech had not come near her: and he said, Lord, wilt thou slay also a righteous nation?",insight:"Abimelech appealed to God's justice, and God listened. Honest pleading is never wasted on the LORD."},
{q:"In what did Abimelech claim he had acted?",options:["In the integrity of his heart and the innocency of his hands","In obedience to his counselors","In ignorance of all law","In reverence for Abraham"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:5",verse:"Said he not unto me, She is my sister? and she, even she herself said, He is my brother: in the integrity of my heart and innocency of my hands have I done this.",insight:"Integrity of heart mattered to God. A clear conscience before God is a strong defense."},
{q:"What did God say He had done for Abimelech?",options:["Withheld him from sinning and not suffered him to touch Sarah","Sent angels to guard his house","Given him a sign in the sky","Struck his servants with fear"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:6",verse:"And God said unto him in a dream, Yea, I know that thou didst this in the integrity of thy heart; for I also withheld thee from sinning against me: therefore suffered I thee not to touch her.",insight:"God restrains sin before we commit it. Much of God's mercy is the evil we never got to do."},
{q:"By what title did God call Abraham here?",options:["A prophet","A priest","A king","A judge"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:7",verse:"Now therefore restore the man his wife; for he is a prophet, and he shall pray for thee, and thou shalt live: and if thou restore her not, know thou that thou shalt surely die, thou, and all that are thine.",insight:"The first \"prophet\" in Scripture is named here. A prophet is one who speaks with God and intercedes for others."},
{q:"What warning came with the command to restore Sarah?",options:["\"If thou restore her not, thou shalt surely die, thou, and all that are thine\"","\"Thy kingdom shall be given to another\"","\"Thy flocks shall perish in a day\"","\"Thou shalt wander as a fugitive\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:7",verse:"Now therefore restore the man his wife; for he is a prophet, and he shall pray for thee, and thou shalt live: and if thou restore her not, know thou that thou shalt surely die, thou, and all that are thine.",insight:"The stakes were total: the king and all his house. Sin against God's people is never a private matter."},
{q:"When did Abimelech act on the dream?",options:["He rose early in the morning and told all his servants","He waited seven days","He sent for Abraham at noon","He fasted for three days first"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:8",verse:"Therefore Abimelech rose early in the morning, and called all his servants, and told all these things in their ears: and the men were sore afraid.",insight:"Early in the morning: conviction that acts quickly. Delayed obedience to a clear word is disobedience."},
{q:"What did Abimelech ask Abraham?",options:["\"What hast thou done unto us? and wherein have I offended thee?\"","\"Why didst thou not trust me?\"","\"What wilt thou require of me?\"","\"Whence camest thou to my land?\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:9",verse:"Then Abimelech called Abraham, and said unto him, What hast thou done unto us? and what have I offended thee, that thou hast brought on me and on my kingdom a great sin? thou hast done deeds unto me that ought not to be done.",insight:"The deceived king rebuked the prophet. When we fail, even unbelievers can see it, and our witness suffers."},
{q:"What had Abraham feared in Gerar?",options:["That the fear of God was not in the place, and they would kill him for his wife","That famine would drive him away","That Abimelech would seize his flocks","That Sarah would be barren forever"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:11",verse:"And Abraham said, Because I thought, Surely the fear of God is not in this place; and they will slay me for my wife’s sake.",insight:"Abraham assumed the worst about Gerar and was wrong; Abimelech proved more honorable than expected. Fear makes poor prophets."},
{q:"What was true about Abraham's claim that Sarah was his sister?",options:["She was his father's daughter, though not his mother's; she became his wife","It was wholly a lie","She was his niece by marriage","She was adopted as his sister"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:12",verse:"And yet indeed she is my sister; she is the daughter of my father, but not the daughter of my mother; and she became my wife.",insight:"Half true is still misleading. Technical truths used to deceive are still deceptions."},
{q:"What had Abraham asked Sarah to do when they began wandering?",options:["To say \"He is my brother\" in every place, as a kindness to him","To hide her beauty with a veil","To claim she was a widow","To stay inside the tent always"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:13",verse:"And it came to pass, when God caused me to wander from my father’s house, that I said unto her, This is thy kindness which thou shalt shew unto me; at every place whither we shall come, say of me, He is my brother.",insight:"A standing arrangement to deceive: Abraham had rehearsed this sin. Preplanned compromise is still compromise."},
{q:"What did Abimelech give Abraham?",options:["Sheep, oxen, menservants, womenservants, and restored his wife","Gold, silver, and chariots","Lands and vineyards","A treaty of peace"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:14",verse:"And Abimelech took sheep, and oxen, and menservants, and womenservants, and gave them unto Abraham, and restored him Sarah his wife.",insight:"The wronged king gave gifts to the wrongdoer. Grace from unexpected hands shames our excuses."},
{q:"What did Abimelech say about the land?",options:["\"Behold, my land is before thee: dwell where it pleaseth thee\"","\"Depart from my borders\"","\"Buy what land thou needest\"","\"Dwell only in Gerar\""],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:15",verse:"And Abimelech said, Behold, my land is before thee: dwell where it pleaseth thee.",insight:"Open land instead of expulsion: mercy wider than deserved. God turned a rebuke into provision."},
{q:"How much silver did Abimelech give for Sarah's vindication?",options:["A thousand pieces of silver","One hundred pieces","Three hundred pieces","Ten thousand pieces"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:16",verse:"And unto Sarah he said, Behold, I have given thy brother a thousand pieces of silver: behold, he is to thee a covering of the eyes, unto all that are with thee, and with all other: thus she was reproved.",insight:"A thousand pieces of silver, \"a covering of the eyes\": public honor restored publicly. God cares about reputations, especially the innocent."},
{q:"What happened when Abraham prayed for Abimelech's house?",options:["God healed Abimelech, his wife, and his maidservants, and they bore children","Fire fell from heaven","The dream came again","Abimelech's wealth was doubled"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 20:17",verse:"So Abraham prayed unto God: and God healed Abimelech, and his wife, and his maidservants; and they bare children.",insight:"The deceiver became the intercessor, and healing flowed. God uses flawed people to bring His wholeness to others."}
]}
]);
